6. Full Psychological Effect Specification
6.1 Psychological Effect Schema
The psychological effect schema defines the structure of a psychological effect deposit.

It has the following fields:

effect_id. A string. Required.

effect_name. A string. Required.

effect_description. A string. Required.

domain. An array of strings. Required.

subdomain. An array of strings. Optional.

original_study. An object. Required. It contains authors, year, journal, title, sample_size, effect_size, confidence_interval, and p_value.

theoretical_basis. An array of strings. Required.

operational_definition. An object. Required. It contains manipulation, measure, and procedure.

moderators. An array of moderator objects. Optional.

boundary_conditions. An array of boundary condition objects. Optional.

replications. An array of replication objects. Optional.

meta_analysis. An object. Optional. It contains authors, year, effect_size, confidence_interval, number_of_studies, and heterogeneity.

replication_status. An enum. Required. The values are not_replicated, replicated, partially_replicated, failed_replication, uncertain.

original_effect_size. An object. Required. It contains value and units.

original_confidence_interval. An object. Optional. It contains lower and upper.

original_p_value. A number. Optional.

meta_analytic_effect_size. An object. Optional. It contains value and units.

meta_analytic_confidence_interval. An object. Optional. It contains lower and upper.

practical_significance. An object. Optional. It contains statement and notes.

related_effects. An array of effect relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

replication_tracker_reference. A string. Optional.

full_pipeline_result_reference. A string. Optional.

null_model_result_reference. A string. Optional.

verification_result_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

The original_study object has:

authors. An array of strings.

year. An integer.

journal. A string.

title. A string.

sample_size. An integer.

effect_size. An object. It contains value and units.

confidence_interval. An object. It contains lower and upper.

p_value. A number.

The operational_definition object has:

manipulation. A string.

measure. A string.

procedure. A string.

Each moderator object has:

moderator_id. A string.

moderator_name. A string.

moderator_description. A string.

moderator_type. An enum. The values are individual_difference, situational, cultural, methodological, other.

effect_direction. An enum. The values are strengthens, weakens, eliminates, reverses, unknown.

Each boundary_condition object has:

condition_id. A string.

condition_name. A string.

condition_description. A string.

condition_type. An enum. The values are population, context, timing, dose, measurement, other.

Each replication object has:

replication_id. A string.

authors. An array of strings.

year. An integer.

journal. A string.

sample_size. An integer.

effect_size. An object. It contains value and units.

confidence_interval. An object. It contains lower and upper.

p_value. A number.

outcome. An enum. The values are success, failure, partial, inconclusive.

preregistration. An enum. The values are preregistered, partially_preregistered, not_preregistered, unknown.

replication_tracker_reference. A string. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

The meta_analysis object has:

authors. An array of strings.

year. An integer.

effect_size. An object. It contains value and units.

confidence_interval. An object. It contains lower and upper.

number_of_studies. An integer.

heterogeneity. An object. It contains I_squared and tau_squared.

Each effect relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_effect_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_domain, same_mechanism, same_measure, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

