7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Psychological Effect
function createPsychologicalEffect(effect, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the effect against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the replication tracker reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the full-pipeline result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. If the null-model result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 7. If the verification result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 8. Generate an effect ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 9. Insert the psychological effect.

Step 10. Insert the moderator records, the boundary condition records, the replication records, and the effect relations.

Step 11. Insert the links if present.

Step 12. Insert the provenance.

Step 13. Insert the moderation record.

Step 14. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 15. Return the effect_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Psychological Effect
function readPsychologicalEffect(effectId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the effect. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the moderators, the boundary conditions, the replications, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Psychological Effect
function updatePsychologicalEffect(effectId, effect, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing effect. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new effect.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the effect_id, the version, and the status updated.

